  "id": "machine-room",
  "name": "Machine Room",
  "tagline": "Machine hum and duct air; the full kit, open hats, claps, toms.",
  "description": "A machine room: a low hum on the root and air rushing through ducts. Four-four kick, sixteenth hats, open hats on the offbeat, claps on two and four, low toms rolling through the bar; a short acid figure underneath.",
  "use": {
    "name": "Energise",
    "for": "Low-energy stretches: the afternoon dip, under-stimulation.",
    "why": "More to hold on to: the busiest drums in the family over a higher, steady noise floor (machine hum and air rushing through ducts). The research's attention-boost profile, a louder noise bed, helps people with inattentive traits a little and slightly hurts others. Reach for it when you are under-stimulated, not as a default."
  },
